git/local
# @summary The clones' directory under the guest's home: the one place in the view that is NOT the view but the guest's own disk -- the image hangs /var/git there (image view write, a nullfs line in fstab), 'guest view mount' makes the mount point, and 'guest repo add' clones into it over ssh. git writes its objects there, which p9fs cannot take (it refuses to create a read-only file for writing). What lies there goes with the disk: 'guest stop' fetches it first (guest repo hold), 'guest drop' refuses without that mark, and 'guest start' clones what the record lists again (guest repo ensure). A path relative to the home.
